# Redis Bonus — WordPress Redis Cache Tests

1. Check Redis container
docker compose ps redis

2. Test Redis server
docker exec redis redis-cli ping

Expected:
PONG

3. Test Redis read/write
docker exec redis redis-cli SET test hello
docker exec redis redis-cli GET test

Expected:
OK
"hello"

Clean the test:
docker exec redis redis-cli DEL test

4. Test WordPress → Redis DNS
docker exec wordpress getent hosts redis

Expected:
Redis container IP address

5. Test WordPress → Redis port
docker exec wordpress bash -c 'cat < /dev/null > /dev/tcp/redis/6379'

Expected:
No error

6. Check PHP Redis extension
docker exec wordpress php -m | grep redis

Expected:
redis

7. Check WordPress Redis host
docker exec wordpress wp config get WP_REDIS_HOST --allow-root --path=/var/www/html

Expected:
redis

8. Check WordPress Redis port
docker exec wordpress wp config get WP_REDIS_PORT --allow-root --path=/var/www/html

Expected:
6379

9. Check WordPress Redis Object Cache
docker exec wordpress wp redis status --allow-root --path=/var/www/html

Expected:
Redis/Object Cache is connected or enabled